{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3423","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3423","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3423\",\"parent_revision\":\"7d96bf8942e91eaf459ae8323cb834a3cc279946a9f08279654742b90786ef3d\",\"root_revision\":\"7d96bf8942e91eaf459ae8323cb834a3cc279946a9f08279654742b90786ef3d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe sub-agent completion contract pins the first line of a worker's final message to `STATUS: DONE | PARTIAL | BLOCKED`. Several dh agents load `dh:subagent-contract` but emit their own domain verdict on that line instead, so a dispatcher branching on the contract tokens matches nothing and cannot tell whether the step succeeded.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: the orchestrator's \\\"did this step succeed?\\\" decision reads a token it does not recognise. It cannot distinguish a completed step from a blocked one for these agents, so it either proceeds past a failed step or stalls on a successful one. Same failure class as the SubagentStop laundering defect fixed in this session, one layer up.\\n\\nExit criterion: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_status_token_vocabulary_drift.py::test_every_status_token_is_registered` passes. That test exists and currently fails; its failure output is the worklist.\\n\\nWorklist as of 2026-09-06 \u2014 5 unregistered tokens across 3 agents:\\n- `STATUS: VERIFIED`, `STATUS: GAPS_FOUND` \u2014 agents/feature-verifier.md\\n- `STATUS: GAPS_FOUND`, `STATUS: CONNECTED` \u2014 agents/integration-checker.md\\n- `STATUS: READY`, `STATUS: DRAFTING` \u2014 agents/plan-validator.md\\n\\nOpen question for grooming: whether these agents report a contract token on the STATUS line and carry their domain verdict on a separate labelled line, or whether the contract admits registered per-agent verdict schemas. The test's `_PINNED_TOKENS` / `_TOLERATED_TOKENS` sets are the single place to encode the answer.\\n\\nAlso in scope: `STATUS: COMPLETE` still has producers in agents/task-worker.md and skills/work-milestone/. Narrowing `_COMPLETE_STATUS_TOKENS` in skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py to the pinned set is the last step and must follow producer conversion, not precede it.\\n\\nSequencing: downstream of agent-orchestration PR #3422, which pins the three-token contract repo-wide.\\n\\nRelated: #2182 covers worker preflight self-check and worker-report structure. This item is narrower \u2014 the token vocabulary itself and its drift guard \u2014 and does not supersede it.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the permissive `DONE|COMPLETE|COMPLETED` matcher in the SubagentStop hook is deliberate temporary breadth carrying a `ponytail:` marker, and stays until this item narrows it. `COMPLETED` was verified to have zero producers anywhere in plugins/ and is accepted defensively only.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: DH delegation-spine audit, session melodic-plotting-emerson (2026-09-06)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"763679a9f6a76d76d9c95b4f2d6c137c3a42e773bfccfbefd7232155dd51d4cc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSzTRpQ\"}"}